---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Lurelia Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Lurelia reminders, routines, habits, journeys, and productivity app."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Lurelia Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: June 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia is a personal productivity and organization application
          designed to help users manage reminders, routines, habits, journeys,
          goals, schedules, and personal progress.
        </p>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains what information Lurelia stores, how it
          is used, and how you remain in control of your information.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data You Create</h2>
        <p>
          Information created within Lurelia may include reminders, recurring
          schedules, habits, routines, journeys, milestones, goals, notes,
          completion history, points, achievements, and user preferences.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information is stored locally on your device and may synchronize
          through your personal iCloud account if CloudKit synchronization is
          enabled.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>iCloud & CloudKit</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia may use Apple's CloudKit framework to synchronize information
          between your Apple devices through your personal iCloud account.
        </p>

        <p>
          The developer of Lurelia does not have access to your private CloudKit
          database.
        </p>

        <p>
          Apple's handling of iCloud data is governed by Apple's privacy policy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Reminders & Scheduling</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia uses local notifications to provide reminder alerts, recurring
          schedules, routine prompts, habit reminders, and journey milestones.
        </p>

        <p>
          Notification scheduling occurs directly on your device and is not
          transmitted to external advertising or marketing services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Habits, Routines & Progress</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia may store completion history, streaks, statistics, progress
          information, and activity records related to habits, routines,
          journeys, and goals.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information exists solely to provide app functionality and
          personal progress tracking.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Journeys & Goals</h2>
        <p>
          If you choose to use journey planning, milestones, objectives,
          timelines, or goal management features, the information you enter is
          stored solely for your personal organization and productivity.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Points, Rewards & Achievements</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia includes optional points, achievements, rewards, streaks, and
          progression systems designed to encourage consistency and motivation.
        </p>

        <p>
          This information remains private to your account and is not used for
          advertising, profiling, or marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Widgets</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia may provide Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets displaying
          reminders, schedules, progress information, habits, routines, points,
          and productivity insights.
        </p>

        <p>
          Widget information is shared locally between the app and widget
          extensions using Apple's App Group system.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Analytics & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia does not use advertising SDKs, targeted advertising
          technologies, or third-party behavioral tracking systems.
        </p>

        <p>
          Lurelia does not sell personal information or share user-generated
          productivity data with advertisers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>In-App Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia may offer optional premium features or subscriptions through
          Apple's StoreKit framework.
        </p>

        <p>
          Payment processing is handled entirely by Apple. Lurelia does not
          collect, store, or have access to payment information, billing
          information, or credit card numbers.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Lurelia is not directed toward children under the age of 13 and does
          not knowingly collect personal information from children.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          You maintain control over your information at all times. Reminders,
          habits, routines, journeys, goals, notes, schedules, and other content
          may be deleted directly within the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          Deleting the app removes locally stored data from your device. If
          CloudKit synchronization is enabled, synced information may also be
          managed through your Apple ID and iCloud settings.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This privacy policy may occasionally be updated to reflect new
          features, legal requirements, platform changes, or improvements to the
          app. Updated versions will be published on this page with a revised
          effective date.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy or how Lurelia handles
          your information, you can contact:
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>
<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>
